## Context
DESIGN-V2 §4 PR-1, honoring R23. Verified defect at edf2748: createSchema
re-stamps SCHEMA_VERSION via INSERT OR REPLACE (sqlite-index.ts:26,153) before
loadMeta ever reads it — the stamp is written and read nowhere, so a downgrade
destroys the evidence of skew at the moment it matters. The PR: read
meta.schemaVersion before any DDL or write; unknown/newer -> sideline the file
(.incompatible-<ts>, never delete), fresh build, one notice. Failing test: open
a fixture stamped schemaVersion=99, assert it is not re-stamped and is
sidelined. Form: PR, no issue (contained defect + failing test — merged twice
per SYNC.md). Send after #20 (same file family).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] failing test demonstrates the re-stamp on a version-99 fixture
- [ ] read-before-write + sideline protocol in the PR, tests green on his tree
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here
